# Floor regression probes — LOCAL ONLY, never committed.
# These files list, in plain text and in ~30 languages, the exact phrasings that
# must be refused, plus every artistic-framing bypass attempt tried against the
# child-safety floor. Every case is blocked, but this repo is public and the
# files would still publish a ready-made prompt list usable against any other
# generator. Keep them on the machine; run them before touching the floor.
tests/floor_*_probe.py

# Prometheus corpus and index — LOCAL ONLY, and large.
# The manifest IS committed (it is the reviewable shelf); the documents are not.
# Several are third-party works whose licences permit a private local copy but
# not redistribution — the Red Cross manual most clearly — so committing the
# corpus to a public repo would be republishing them. Everything here is
# reproducible with ./fetch.sh from the manifest.
prometheus/corpus/
prometheus/index.db
prometheus/index.db-wal
prometheus/index.db-shm

# Security audit — LOCAL ONLY. Documents open findings on a live, internet-
# reachable host; publishing it hands over a current vulnerability map.
docs/security_audit_*.md
